+## Trunkline macOS coordinate adaptation
+
+The Trunkline backend adaptation interprets absolute mouse coordinates within the logical bounding rectangle of all active displays. Coordinates are normalized from the caller-provided dimensions, then translated by the desktop origin. Buttons following absolute motion use the last requested target, even before WindowServer has processed it. Relative motion switches back to the current global position and clamps to the nearest active screen rather than the primary monitor. Display topology is cached and refreshed on CoreGraphics reconfiguration callbacks. Consumers must supply matching global desktop metadata; this patch must be paired with Trunkline’s capture-geometry patch.
